# Language policy

## After prompt87 Phase B (2026-07-22)

| Layer | Language | Examples |
|-------|----------|----------|
| **Language gate + Quick Start** | **`appLocale`** (`userLanguage`) | Wizard copy, units row labels, help `?` → `/{lang}/help/` |
| **Dashboard chrome** | **`appLocale`** | Strip titles, Food Log, Profile nested labels, status/ago, dates |
| **Coach & meals & exports** | **`appLocale`** | Gemini chat, meal `name_local`, visit reports |
| **Clinic portal UI** | **English** | Clinician tool |
| **Website help** | **Path locale** | `https://healthings.ai/{en\|he\|es\|fr\|de\|ar\|ru}/help/…` |

## Always-English glossary

Brand, units (`kcal`, `mg/dL`, `kg`), acronyms (`CGM`, `BMR`, `AI`), device names (Withings…), slash commands. Profile nested titles use bare nouns (Profile / Targets…), not “My …” product phrases.

## Settings UX

One language preference drives coach, meals, Quick Start, help links, and dashboard chrome. Prefer **App & coach language** when touching the Profile picker label.

## RTL

Hebrew/Arabic: RTL for Quick Start and user-content areas (chat, meals, exports). Dashboard strip structure stays LTR chrome with localized strings; full layout RTL is deferred.

## Intent detection

Chat slash commands and natural-language triggers may stay multilingual (`chatIntent.ts`).

## When to revisit

Clinic portal i18n (Phase C) if clinicians need non-English UI. Full chrome RTL if Hebrew/Arabic users need mirrored strip layout.
